WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.637
Telo Ride 1 has no menu. Open it with a paired bike, and the first thing you see is

00:00:07.637 --> 00:00:08.546
the class.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.154
Four screens are left: connect the bike, the class, the ride, and the result. Done

00:00:15.154 --> 00:00:18.163
and Ride it again both lead back to the class.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.317
Home, Profile, Settings, Diagnostics and the class library are gone. Their old

00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:32.923
addresses say the page does not exist, and lead back to the class.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.912
With no settings, the app decides. The screen stays awake, the theme follows the

00:00:40.912 --> 00:00:44.258
device, and heart rate and the packet log left too.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.213
The class at the root address, on every screen from a phone to a desktop.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.431
What the tests prove: no navigation, four old addresses not found, and every check

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.833
still passes, in a smaller bundle.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.920
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.116
nothing else.

00:01:19.461 --> 00:01:24.413
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:29.425
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:32.926
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:37.247
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
